===Group B===
{{Main|1978 FIFA World Cup Group B}}

Argentina had qualified for the second group stage after obtaining second place in Group 1 behind Italy while Brazil had also obtained the second position of Group 3 after [[Austria national football team|Austria]]. Both Peru and [[Poland national football team|Poland]] had achieved first place in Group 4 and Group 2 respectively. The headquarters of this group were [[Mendoza, Argentina|Mendoza]] and [[Rosario]].

The first game pitted Brazil against Peru, ending with a 3–0 victory for the Brazilians.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://es.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/edition=50/results/matches/match=2251/report.html |title=Match Report: Brasil – Perú |website=FIFA|access-date=July 11, 2010|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090202051036/http://es.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/edition%3D50/results/matches/match%3D2251/report.html|archive-date=February 2, 2009}}</ref> Argentina also beat Poland 2–0 in Rosario with two goals from [[Mario Kempes]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://es.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/edition=50/results/matches/match=2202/report.html |title=Match Report: Argentina – Polonia |author=FIFA|access-date=July 11, 2010|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111218061222/http://es.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/edition%3D50/results/matches/match%3D2202/report.html|archive-date=December 18, 2011}}</ref> The victory of Poland over Peru by 1–0<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://es.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/edition=50/results/matches/match=2450/report.html |title=Match Report: Polonia – Perú |website=FIFA|access-date=July 11, 2010|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111218064846/http://es.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/edition%3D50/results/matches/match%3D2450/report.html|archive-date=December 18, 2011}}</ref> and the goalless draw between Argentina and Brazil<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://es.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/edition=50/results/matches/match=2196/report.html |title=Match Report: Argentina – Brasil |website=FIFA|access-date=July 11, 2010|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110927074846/http://es.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/edition%3D50/results/matches/match%3D2196/report.html|archive-date=September 27, 2011}}</ref> left a group close in which, with the exception of Peru, the other three teams had a chance to reach the final. Argentina and Brazil reached the last game with 3 points, although the Brazilians had a greater goal difference. Poland arrived with 2 points but with chances to win the group if, after their victory, Argentina lost or tied without surpassing it in goal difference.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Sosa |first=Zaritzi |title=Mundial 1978: la verdadera historia de la sospechosa goleada de Argentina 6–0 vs Perú |url=https://www.tudn.com/futbol/mundial-qatar-2022/historia-mundiales/mundial-1978-la-verdadera-historia-de-la-sospechosa-goleada-de-argentina-6-0-vs-peru |date=May 25, 2022 |website=[[TUDN (Mexican TV channel)|TUDN]] |language=es|access-date=February 12, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221222021859/https://www.tudn.com/futbol/mundial-qatar-2022/historia-mundiales/mundial-1978-la-verdadera-historia-de-la-sospechosa-goleada-de-argentina-6-0-vs-peru|archive-date=December 22, 2022}}</ref>

The matches were not played at the same time but Brazil and Poland played first at 16:45 while Argentina and Peru did so later, at 19:15. Brazil won their match 3–1, with two goals from [[Roberto Dinamite]] and one from [[Nelinho]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://es.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/edition=50/results/matches/match=2252/report.html |title=Match Report: Brasil – Polonia |author=FIFA|access-date=July 11, 2010|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111218063742/http://es.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/edition%3D50/results/matches/match%3D2252/report.html|archive-date=December 18, 2011}}</ref> With this result they finished with 5 points and +5 goal difference. In order to reach the final, Argentina had to win with a margin of four goals since they had a goal difference of +2.<ref name="Yahoo!">{{Cite web |title=Argentina's 1978 World Cup win against Peru was fixed in a brutal political deal, former senator says |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/ro-rogers_argentina_peru_fixing_scandal_world_cup_021012.html?guccounter=1&guce_referrer=aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbS8&guce_referrer_sig=AQAAAAmI_7MjQiiIaYPPiIrYecPDPQEjTQ9h6xFnHS6mutKre0_uw5nMms4nOwkxnX4AUiHfzxXN4yx2_oQbO7Hhve0rdUMWNKmlA9LCwYlUQrqAGn0qGZqkoJ3R2IYRUGDsVbZNL8fh4ufsIgVr-p95NitADypjGaiYMfbIz6HOzTby |website=[[Yahoo! Sports]] |date=11 February 2012 |language=en-us|access-date=February 12, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Exposing The Myth: Why The 1978 World Cup In Argentina Should Never Have Been Played |url=https://www.thesportsman.com/articles/exposing-the-myth-why-the-1978-world-cup-in-argentina-should-never-have-been-played |website=The Sportsman |date=25 June 2019 |language=en|access-date=February 12, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220908034621/https://www.thesportsman.com/articles/exposing-the-myth-why-the-1978-world-cup-in-argentina-should-never-have-been-played|archive-date=September 8, 2022}}</ref> Argentina managed to prevail over Peru by 6–0 and thus qualified for the final.<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://es.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/edition=50/results/matches/match=2201/report.html |title=Match Report: Argentina – Perú |author=FIFA|access-date=July 11, 2010|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090202042457/http://es.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/edition%3D50/results/matches/match%3D2201/report.html|archive-date=February 2, 2009}}</ref>

